# Build-time configuration for the Belmont News app.
#
# Names only. The real values live in Paperclip's secret store, and must be
# added to this repository as Actions secrets before the Pages deploy can run:
#
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL          the project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY     the RLS-facing anon key
#
# The anon key is publishable by design — it is the key browsers are meant to
# send, and RLS is what protects the data — but it still belongs in the secret
# store, not in this repository. The `service_role` key is never publishable and
# must never be set here; it bypasses RLS.
#
# `VITE_`-prefixed values are inlined into the client bundle at build time, which
# is why the anon key and not the service_role key is the one that belongs here.
#
# The Pages deploy also sets BASE_PATH=/belmont/ in the workflow itself. That one
# is not a secret and not an app variable: it is the path prefix the built app
# is served from, and it is `/` on the Bolt host.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
